Lora Config Parameters:
   r=8. Rank: Controls the size of the LoRA adapter matrices
Basically: how much the model is allowed to “learn new patterns”
In general 8 is the good rank for the model

lora_alpha: Scaling Factor
How Strongly Lora updates effect the model
Relation ship with R: Effective strength= lora_Aplha/r
if the values higher value: Stornger inluence on finetuning
Too High value: Unstable Training (Overfitting)
Too Low Value: Model doesn't learn Much (underfitting)

lora_dropout=0.05
Randomly drops some Lora connections during training
It prevents overfittimg
Makes Model generalize better

target_models="all-linear"
tell lora which layers to modify
LLMs have may layers: Attention, feedforward, backpropogation etc
"all-linear" → apply LoRA to all linear layers
More coverage → better learning
Slightly more compute
"q_proj", "v_proj" → only attention layers
More efficient but less expressive

task_type = "CAUSAL_LM"
Defines the type of model task
"CAUSAL_LM" means:
Predict next word based on previous words
Used for:
Chatbots, text generation, Q&A system

Different tasks require different training logic:

"CAUSAL_LM" → GPT-style models
"SEQ_2_SEQ_LM" → T5/BART (input → output transformation)

Hugging Transformer Pipeline API: to run the LLM in easiest possibile way
Ready made wrapper consistf of model, tokenizer, data processing(preprocessing or post processing)
